! =====================================================================
!  inxflow600_circ_pcbench
!  Two-arm benchmark for the physics PC (docs/physics_pc).
!
!  This is the physics of the maintained regression test
!  `reg_tests/testcases/inxflow_600_vpar_T_all` -- a ballooning-unstable
!  pedestal, ZK_par = 100, ohmic heating, edge and gaussian sources --
!  ported onto model199 (so: WITHOUT parallel velocity) and onto the
!  CIRCULAR geometry of `namelist/model199/inxflow_circ_pcbench`.
!
!  Why the port is nearly free: model199 IS model600's base model.  Both
!  declare n_var = 6 with the same slots
!      var_psi=1  var_u=2  var_zj=3  var_w=4  var_rho=5  var_T=6
!  (models/model199/mod_model_settings.f90 vs models/model600/
!  mod_model_settings.f90, n_var_base = 6).  The regression test just
!  switches on the i_ext_vpar extension, giving a 7th variable.  Dropping
!  v_par is exactly what model199 already is.
!
!  Purpose: every PC measurement so far comes from
!  `intear_pcbench_gradients` -- a 2/1 tearing mode, n = 1, very large
!  aspect ratio, low beta.  This is the opposite corner, and it is run as
!  a full time loop with two arms (physics PC vs. baseline), not as a
!  single-step verify_schur diagnostic.
!
!  --- What did NOT survive the port ------------------------------------
!  Entries of the 600 test that model199's namelist does not declare.
!  Leaving any of them in makes the read(42,in1) abort:
!
!    tgnum_psi/u/zj/w/rho/T/vpar
!        model199 declares only the indexed `tgnum`, and its element
!        matrices never reference it -- only model600/mod_elt_matrix_fft.f90
!        implements Taylor-Galerkin stabilisation.  So this case has NO TG
!        stabilisation at all; eta_num and visco_num have to carry that
!        load.  Watch for it if the run gets noisy at tstep = 3.
!    visco_old_setup      (model600-only; the old R^2-dependent viscosity)
!    eta_coul_log_dep     (model600-only; model199 has eta_T_dependent)
!    min_sheath_angle     (model600-only; model199 has gamma_sheath /
!                          density_reflection, and there is no sheath here
!                          anyway -- circular limiter, no open region)
!
!  Accepted by the namelist but INERT under model199, so set explicitly or
!  dropped rather than left looking meaningful:
!
!    visco_par, visco_par_num  -- with_Vpar = .false., never used
!    tauIC                     -- not referenced by model199
!    bootstrap                 -- model199's element matrices never call
!                                 bootstrap_current (only 303/501/600/710/
!                                 711 do).  Set .f.
!    NEO, aki_neo_const, amu_neo_const
!                              -- neoclassical coefficients are consumed by
!                                 the v_par equation.  Set NEO = .f.
!    bc_natural_open           -- meaningless with n_open/n_leg/n_private = 0
!
!  Note also that `zkpar_T_dependent` is in the namelist but unused in
!  model199, so ZK_par stays constant -- ZK_par = 100 does not run away.
!
!  --- Geometry ---------------------------------------------------------
!  CIRCULAR LIMITER, unchanged from inxflow_circ_pcbench.  A diverted mesh
!  would put `eliminate_boundary_dofs` -- which every measurement in this
!  study depends on -- on open field lines, where it is untested.
!
!  --- How the drive was found (measured, do not re-derive) -------------
!  Circularizing removes the separatrix flux expansion that gives the
!  original X-point case its peeling-BALLOONING drive, and model199 also
!  never calls bootstrap_current, so there is no edge current for the
!  peeling half either.  n = 6 is consequently IDEAL-STABLE here, and no
!  pressure/q knob recovers it.  Measured, each from its own stage 1,
!  ~60-115 steps at tstep = 3, growth reported as (gamma_mag, gamma_kin):
!
!    baseline                          beta_N 2.33%  (+4.2e-3, +3.4e-3)
!    T_coef(4) 0.08 -> 0.04            beta_N 2.32%  (-8.3e-3, -1.2e-2)
!    T_0     1.5d-2 -> 4.5d-2          beta_N 4.25%  (-2.4e-2, -1.0e-2)
!    F0         3.0 -> 4.5             beta_N 1.55%  (+2.1e-2, -4.7e-4)
!    the first two combined            beta_N 4.23%  (-1.7e-2, +8.4e-3)
!    X-POINT geometry restored         beta_N 1.91%  (-1.1e-2, -5.7e-3)
!
!  In every one of those the magnetic and kinetic growth rates disagree in
!  SIGN and the energies sit at 1e-25..1e-26 -- that is the seed decaying,
!  not a mode.  Note the X-point row: even restoring the diverted geometry
!  did not help, which is what points at the missing bootstrap current.
!
!  What DOES work is RESISTIVITY -- the physical eta, not eta_num (eta_num
!  is dissipative, it damps small scales and can never drive anything).
!  Raising eta 2.d-6 -> 2.d-5 excites a clean n = 6 RESISTIVE mode in the
!  circular geometry:
!
!    E_kin(n=6) 3.1e-26 -> 3.0e-19 over steps 81..181  (7 decades)
!    gamma*tau_A = 2.66e-2, constant to 3 significant figures
!
!  That is the drive this case uses, and it is why `eta` below is 2.d-5
!  and not the 2.d-6 of the 600 test.  The mode is resistive rather than
!  ideal-ballooning; the pedestal, the ZK_par = 100 anisotropy and the
!  sources are still those of the 600 test.
!
!  Keeping the geometry circular is what makes this worth it:
!  `eliminate_boundary_dofs` stays valid (no open field lines), so these
!  numbers remain comparable with the whole earlier tearing sweep.
!
!  --- Mesh -------------------------------------------------------------
!  Coarsened from inxflow_circ_pcbench's 81x128 / 40x64 to ~3000 DOF per
!  variable, so a several-hundred-step run of BOTH arms fits on the single
!  MPI rank the physics PC apply path requires.
!
!  --- Compile-time settings --------------------------------------------
!  n_tor / n_period / n_plane live in models/mod_settings.f90, NOT here.
!  Two builds:
!    stage 1, axisymmetric :  ./util/config.sh model=199 n_tor=1 n_period=1 n_plane=1
!    stage 2/3, ballooning :  ./util/config.sh model=199 n_tor=3 n_period=6 n_plane=4
!  models/det_modes.f90:13 is mode(itor) = int(itor/2)*n_period, so
!  n_tor=3, n_period=6 gives exactly n = 0 and n = 6.
!
!  --- Workflow ---------------------------------------------------------
!  Stage 1 MUST ramp the time step.  Starting straight at tstep = 3 blows
!  the run up within ~25 steps -- and JOREK still exits 0 while writing NaN
!  restart files, so the failure is silent.
!
!    ./util/setinput.sh inxflow600_circ_pcbench \
!        tstep_n=1.d-3,1.d-2,1.d-1,1.d0,3.d0 nstep_n=10,10,10,10,10 \
!        restart=.f. nout=5
!    mpirun -n 1 ./jorek_model199_ntor1 < inxflow600_circ_pcbench
!
!  Stage 2 (new harmonics seeded at 1e-10 * the axisymmetric rho and T by
!  mod_import_restart.f90; the log's "Increasing number of harmonics from
!  1 to 3!" warning is correct):
!
!    ./util/setinput.sh inxflow600_circ_pcbench tstep_n=3.d0 nstep_n=1000 restart=.t. nout=25
!    mpirun -n 1 ./jorek_model199 < inxflow600_circ_pcbench
!    egrep 'W_mag,_kin|Growth_mag,_kin' log_stage2 | tail -20
!
!  Stage 3, the two arms: copy this file into run_s65_pc/ and run_s65_std/
!  with the stage-2 restart, and change ONLY the physics-PC block at the
!  bottom.  `diff` the two `in` files to prove nothing else moved.
!
!  Run on 1 MPI rank: the physics PC apply path fails for np > 1
!  (pre-existing, independent of this work).  OpenMP threads are fine.
! =====================================================================

&in1

 restart = .f.
 regrid  = .f.

 tstep_n   = 1.d-3,1.d-2,1.d-1,1.d0,3.d0
 nstep_n   = 10,10,10,10,10

 nout = 5

 n_tor_fft_thresh = 2

 freeboundary = .f.

 fbnd(1)   = 2.
 fbnd(2:4) = 0.
 mf        = 0

! --- circular limiter geometry ---------------------------------------
 ellip  = 1.
 tria_u = 0.
 tria_l = 0.
 quad_u = 0.
 quad_l = 0.

 xpoint = .f.
 xampl  = 0.
 xsig   = 0.6
 xwidth = 1.5
 xtheta = 4.7
 xshift = 0.0

 R_begin = 2.9
 R_end   = 3.1
 Z_begin = -0.1
 Z_end   = 0.1

 R_geo = 3.0
 Z_geo = 0.
 amin  = 1.

 F0    = 3.0

! --- mesh: ~3000 DOF/variable, both arms must fit on 1 rank -----------
 n_R      = 0
 n_Z      = 0
 n_radial = 41
 n_pol    = 64

 n_flux    = 24
 n_tht     = 32
 n_open    = 0
 n_leg     = 0
 n_private = 0

! --- transport, from inxflow_600_vpar_T_all --------------------------
! eta is the ONE value deliberately changed from the 600 test (2.d-6):
! it is the drive.  See "How the drive was found" in the header.
 eta       = 2.d-5
 eta_ohmic = 1.d-7
 visco     = 4.d-6

! numerical dissipation: with no Taylor-Galerkin term in model199 this is
! the only stabilisation this case has
 eta_num   = 3.d-10
 visco_num = 1.d-11

 D_par     = 0.d0
 D_perp(1) = 1.d-5
 D_perp(2) = 0.85d0
 D_perp(3) = 0.d0
 D_perp(4) = 0.01d0
 D_perp(5) = 0.92d0

 ZK_par     = 100.d0
 ZK_perp(1) = 1.d-5
 ZK_perp(2) = 0.85d0
 ZK_perp(3) = 0.d0
 ZK_perp(4) = 0.01d0
 ZK_perp(5) = 0.92d0

! --- equilibrium ------------------------------------------------------
 FF_0 = 1.6
 FF_1 = 0.
 FF_coef(1)  = -1.0
 FF_coef(2)  = 0.d0
 FF_coef(3)  = 0.d0
 FF_coef(4)  = 0.03d0
 FF_coef(5)  = 1.0d0
 FF_coef(6)  = -0.06d0
 FF_coef(7)  = 0.90d0
 FF_coef(8)  = 0.07d0

 T_0 = 1.5d-2
 T_1 = 3.d-4
 T_coef(1) = -0.66d0
 T_coef(2) = +0.0d0
 T_coef(3) = 0.d0
 T_coef(4) = 0.08d0
 T_coef(5) = 0.94d0

 rho_0 = 1.
 rho_1 = 0.01
 rho_coef(1)  =  0.0
 rho_coef(2)  =  0.0
 rho_coef(3)  =  0.0
 rho_coef(4)  =  0.08
 rho_coef(5)  =  0.94d0

! --- sources ----------------------------------------------------------
 heatsource                = 1.d-7
 particlesource            = 5.d-6
 edgeparticlesource        = 1.d-7
 edgeparticlesource_psin   = 1.d0
 edgeparticlesource_sig    = 0.03d0
 particlesource_gauss      = 1.d-7
 particlesource_gauss_psin = 0.d0
 particlesource_gauss_sig  = 0.1d0
 heatsource_gauss          = 1.d-8
 heatsource_gauss_psin     = 0.d0
 heatsource_gauss_sig      = 0.1d0

! Present in the 600 test, but model199 implements neither: its element
! matrices never call bootstrap_current, and the neoclassical coefficients
! are consumed by the v_par equation that this model does not have.
 bootstrap = .f.
 NEO       = .f.

! --- solver -----------------------------------------------------------
 iter_precon    = 22
 gmres_m        = 20
 gmres_4        = 1.d0
 gmres_max_iter = 200
 gmres_tol      = 1.d-8

! --- physics PC -------------------------------------------------------
! Eliminate the Dirichlet DOFs (row+column zeroed, representative diagonal)
! instead of the 1e12 ZBIG penalty.  Wanted for the PC study: the penalty
! rows otherwise dominate every operator norm.
!
! CAUTION: this flag is ours, it is in no stock JOREK case, and it is applied
! to the MAIN system matrix (matrix/construct_matrix_mod.f90:474-748), not
! only to the PC matrices -- so it changes the boundary condition of the
! physics solve.  Keep it OFF for the stage-1/stage-2 physics runs; for the
! stage-3 two-arm comparison it must be ON and IDENTICAL in both arms, or
! the two arms are not solving the same problem.
 eliminate_boundary_dofs      = .f.

 use_physics_pc               = .f.
 debug_physics_pc             = .f.
 physics_pc_monolithic        = .f.
 physics_pc_multi_step        = .t.
 physics_pc_wave_schur        = .t.
 physics_pc_schur_channels    = 1
 physics_pc_schur_massinv     = 8
 physics_pc_reduced_pde       = .f.
 physics_pc_drop_psi_coupling = .f.
 physics_pc_verify_reduced    = .f.

! this build has no MUMPS/STRUMPACK bindings; MUMPS is reached via PETSc
 use_strumpack     = .f.
 use_strumpack_eq  = .f.
 use_strumpack_prj = .f.
 use_mumps         = .f.
 use_mumps_eq      = .f.
 use_mumps_prj     = .f.
 use_pastix        = .f.
 use_pastix_eq     = .f.
 use_pastix_prj    = .f.
 use_petsc_eq      = .t.
/
